{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784624043,"nonce":"EJfBopPJh/FwpatX79/QQk02ugk=","title":"Sidecar service, end-to-end","message":"## Parent\nEpic 01c81a5\n\n## What to build\nThe default Service form, complete. A `services:` field on a Step declares throwaway backing containers co-located INSIDE that Step's Pod, reachable at `localhost:\u003cport\u003e`, alive only for that Step's execution (reuses the ADR-0042 native-sidecar pattern — initContainer restartPolicy:Always). Includes a `ready:` probe schema (tcp default; exec/http) wired to the sidecar startup probe so the Step's main container does not start until the service is ready. Service containers run under the ADR-0039 restricted baseline; `run-as-root` self-service grant applies for stock DB images.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `services:` field parses + validates in the pipeline IR (scarab-pipeline)\n- [ ] k8s executor injects the sidecar container(s) into the Step's Pod; local executor does the same on kind\n- [ ] `ready:` probe (tcp default) gates the main container start\n- [ ] Sidecar container inherits the ADR-0039 restricted baseline; grants applicable\n- [ ] Unit test asserting the built Pod spec contains the co-located container + probe (no live cluster needed)\n\n## Blocked by\nNone - can start immediately","files":null}]}